        "hash": "5aac38327349ed7089d262b3a8173e1ed794c1d3",
        "subject": "wip(local-book): preserve streaming XHTML optimization for repair",
        "body": "Archive the existing 128 KiB html5ever tokenizer path, linear anchor-offset\nmapping, and character-count optimizations as a separate work-in-progress\nchange. This commit preserves prior work; it is not an accepted parser fix.\n\nFour isolated production-entrypoint threshold probes reproduce regressions:\n- HTML <br> loses its line break above the threshold.\n- A script string containing <style> suppresses subsequent visible body text.\n- textarea raw text is interpreted as HTML structure.\n- Navigation anchors after the first 4096 are silently discarded.\n\nThe existing reader-local-book suite passes 253 tests, but those checks do\nnot cover these failures. Do not treat this commit, a green standard suite,\nor any earlier HAP/VM result as delivery or acceptance evidence. Repair and\nrerun the differential probes before using this path in a validated build.\n\nRaw workspace evidence:\n../evidence/local-book-oss-implementation/streaming-xhtml-commit-review.json\n../evidence/local-book-oss-implementation/streaming-xhtml-commit-review.log\n../evidence/local-book-oss-implementation/streaming-xhtml-commit-review-probes.rs",
